  "grammar": [
    {
      "title": "Dative subject: 'I want', 'I like', 'I'm hungry'",
      "body": "Many feelings and needs are expressed with the experiencer in the **dative case (-க்கு)** and the thing as the grammatical subject:\n\n**எனக்கு காபி வேணும்** — to-me coffee is-wanted → 'I want coffee'\n**எனக்கு காபி பிடிக்கும்** — to-me coffee is-pleasing → 'I like coffee'\n**எனக்குப் பசிக்குது** — to-me (it) hungers → 'I'm hungry'\n\nThe verb doesn't change for person: வேணும், பிடிக்கும் stay the same whoever wants or likes. Negatives: **வேணாம்** 'don't want', **பிடிக்காது** 'don't like'. Questions: வேணுமா? பிடிக்குமா?\n\n(A hard consonant after -க்கு is often doubled in writing — எனக்குப் பசி *enakkup pasi* — this is sandhi; in casual speech it is weak or dropped, and many people leave it out when writing spoken Tamil.)",
      "examples": [
        { "native": "உங்களுக்கு என்ன வேணும்?", "roman": "ungaḷukku enna vēṇum?", "en": "What would you like?" },
        { "native": "அவருக்கு டீ வேணாம்.", "roman": "avarukku ṭī vēṇām.", "en": "He doesn't want tea." },
        { "native": "உங்களுக்குக் காரம் பிடிக்குமா?", "roman": "ungaḷukkuk kāram piḍikkumā?", "en": "Do you like spicy food?" },
        { "native": "குழந்தைக்குப் பசிக்குது.", "roman": "kuḻandaikkup pasikkudu.", "en": "The baby is hungry." },
        { "native": "எனக்கு இனிப்பு பிடிக்காது.", "roman": "enakku inippu piḍikkādu.", "en": "I don't like sweets." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Ordering politely with குடுங்க",
      "body": "In restaurants and shops you simply name the item and add **குடுங்க** *kuḍunga* 'please give' (written கொடுங்கள்). Adding **கொஞ்சம்** *konjam* 'a little' softens any request: கொஞ்சம் தண்ணி குடுங்க.\n\nTo ask whether something is available, use **இருக்கா?** *irukkā?* 'is there?'. The answer is **இருக்கு** 'there is' or **இல்ல** 'there isn't'. 'Give me … more' is **இன்னும் … குடுங்க**.",
      "examples": [
        { "native": "ஒரு மசாலா தோசை குடுங்க.", "roman": "oru masālā dōsai kuḍunga.", "en": "One masala dosa, please." },
        { "native": "பூரி இருக்கா?", "roman": "pūri irukkā?", "en": "Do you have puri?" },
        { "native": "இல்ல சார், முடிஞ்சு போச்சு.", "roman": "illa sār, muḍinju pōcchu.", "en": "No sir, it's finished." },
        { "native": "இன்னும் கொஞ்சம் சாம்பார் குடுங்க.", "roman": "innum konjam sāmbār kuḍunga.", "en": "A bit more sambar, please." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "dialogue": {
    "title": "Breakfast at a tiffin centre",
    "setting": "Tom and his friend Karthik sit down at a busy vegetarian restaurant in the morning.",
    "lines": [
      { "speaker": "Waiter", "native": "என்ன சாப்பிடுறீங்க சார்?", "roman": "enna sāppiḍurīnga sār?", "en": "What will you have, sir?" },
      { "speaker": "Karthik", "native": "டிஃபன் என்ன இருக்கு?", "roman": "ṭifan enna irukku?", "en": "What's there for tiffin?" },
      { "speaker": "Waiter", "native": "இட்லி, தோசை, பொங்கல், பூரி இருக்கு.", "roman": "iḍli, dōsai, pongal, pūri irukku.", "en": "There's idli, dosa, pongal and puri." },
      { "speaker": "Karthik", "native": "எனக்கு ரெண்டு இட்லி, ஒரு வடை. டாம், உங்களுக்கு?", "roman": "enakku reṇḍu iḍli, oru vaḍai. Ṭām, ungaḷukku?", "en": "Two idlis and a vadai for me. Tom, for you?" },
